{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1402704-as-a-mentor-a-question-get-a-watsonian-answer","id":1402704,"title":"As a Mentor a Question, Get a Watsonian Answer","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-13T17:48:21-07:00","id":1402704,"title":"As a Mentor a Question, Get a Watsonian Answer","content":"I hope this was a good idea! It occurred to me that a lot of the debates and questions on this forum tend to be Doylist and need Doylist answers, answers useful for acting as the Storyteller or knowing how stuff works independent of Mages hang-ups. Just a few things I've seen around here is the Duat/Lower Depth topic, the topic of how Quiescence should or shouldn't activate when trying to use magic in public, and things of that sort. Mage players have a vested interest in knowing how stuff works to make our games internally consistent, and faithful to the books.<br /> <br /> But the Mages themselves don't have it that easy! When Mages have questions they either answer it themselves or ask someone else, and the game wouldn't be interesting if Mages could be wrong/duped or just flat out opinionated.<br /> <br /> So I'd like to do a fun cooperative experiment here~ This will be a topic specifically about <i>how</i> Mages get their answers in-universe, particularly from their mentors and teachers. We the forum-users ask a Doylist question, and whoever answers should give the answer that another Mage would give--in other words, you <i>don't have to be correct.</i><br /> <br /> This will be for people who want examples and ideas of how Mages give in-game explanations of how things work, including their personal hang-ups and theories, answers that help make playing Mage more interesting and offer new ideas on how to diversify our games, an exploration of not only how our trusted Mentors can help us... and mislead us.<br /> <br /> I'll start with some low hanging fruit.<br /> <br /> How come Shadow Flesh can transform a Mage into an actual shadow with Death alone, instead of Death+Life? This one creeps up again sometimes as we get new users, so its a great question to ask a hypothetical answer so we can see some interesting in-character answers.<br /> <br /> So what if my mentor is an Obrimos? I'll respond to my own question for example, and have the Obrimos say... &quot;Death is the Inferior Arcanum of the Aether, that is to say, Truth cannot die, but can be suppressed and hidden. Such a spell is ostensibly Patterning, but is used like a veiling spell. The Mage is quite literally hiding the Truth of their body behind a patterned curtain of the Death arcanum, leaving nothing else to see. Course it would have been <i>easier</i> to simply study the Forces Arcanum...!&quot;<br /> <br /> So my Obrimos <i>thinks </i>this spell works by hiding other symbols in the subject's pattern behind the Death-spell itself, like a curtain, leaving only a shadow left. But an Acanthus might answer differently!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-14T11:34:25-07:00","id":1402843,"title":"","content":"&quot;For most people, death is how an individual's story ends. But it can also serve a higher purpose in a tale. Remember how the angel of death comes to Scrooge as a shadow or how the heroes in the monomyth return from the Underworld. Death can be transformative, not merely an end. If only the script tells the actor must face it to be reforged by it.<br /> <br /> But the Awakened are not mere actors, they are directors. The skilled practicioner of this Arcana can walk in the liminal realm between states, to command the tapestry to let them dip into the waters of the Styx without being drowned in it. The potential for the scene was always in our path towards the finale, but a Patterning lets them call it forth, redefine it, coreograph it&quot;- <i>An Acanthus' response</i><br /> <br /> <b>Question:</b> Rotes are a more refined way to cast particular spells, but why do they de-personalize the Nimbus of the caster ? They are created by an in depth study of the spell, filtered by the symbolism of a certain skill. But that requires the mage to explore that symbolism. But doesn't that make them a representation of their comprehension of it ? Then wouldn't it necessarily be colored by their personality and Watchtower, since they invested so much of their time, Will and focus into crafting it ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-14T11:53:27-07:00","id":1402846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1402704-as-a-mentor-a-question-get-a-watsonian-answer?p=1402843#post1402843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Question:</b> Rotes are a more refined way to cast particular spells, but why do they de-personalize the Nimbus of the caster ? They are created by an in depth study of the spell, filtered by the symbolism of a certain skill. But that requires the mage to explore that symbolism. But doesn't that make them a representation of their comprehension of it ? Then wouldn't it necessarily be colored by their personality and Watchtower, since they invested so much of their time, Will and focus into crafting it ?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Just as the Dukes and Duchesses of the spirit courts can forge lasting sources of the Resonance that sustains their own Manifestations as well as those of their servants, Masters of an Arcanum crafting rotes shorten the distance between Supernal Truth and the spells they put their time and training into. It's nothing on the level of Imperial sorcery, but rotecraft builds new symbols into the boundary between the real and the ideal that let certain Truths cross the Abyss more easily. Gnosis is personal, but an Instrument is an Instrument, and mudras' use extends beyond their creators.&quot;<br /> <br /> Why does a person's daimon seem to defend their Oneiros with goetia representing their weaknesses more than their points of strength?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-14T12:41:35-07:00","id":1402853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1402704-as-a-mentor-a-question-get-a-watsonian-answer?p=1402846#post1402846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Just as the Dukes and Duchesses of the spirit courts can forge lasting sources of the Resonance that sustains their own Manifestations as well as those of their servants, Masters of an Arcanum crafting rotes shorten the distance between Supernal Truth and the spells they put their time and training into. It's nothing on the level of Imperial sorcery, but rotecraft builds new symbols into the boundary between the real and the ideal that let certain Truths cross the Abyss more easily. Gnosis is personal, but an Instrument is an Instrument, and mudras' use extends beyond their creators.&quot;<br /> <br /> Why does a person's daimon seem to defend their Oneiros with goetia representing their weaknesses more than their points of strength?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;A person's weaknesses are the most powerful tools that they possess. What defines us more in our minds? We torment ourselves daily with what we fail to accomplish, chiding our laziness, our own incompetence, our inability to achieve our dreams. We blame some demon for our foils, and oh, how strong that demon must be to shackle our capability so! And that is why our souls use these goetia for its defense, for what greater power do we have than the powers we've tenderly fed with all our doubts, fears and disappointment? And people's weaknesses are well fed indeed, are they not?&quot; - Daniel the Blackiron, Mastigos<br /> <br /> <br /> Why does Prime have nothing to do with the soul?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-14T13:45:37-07:00","id":1402861,"title":"","content":"&quot;It seems so, but in fact, as Prime purview includes Truth, what could be more true than people soul?<br /> The implication of this concept is that souls are made of symbols of Truth, in other words of Mana!<br /> And of course i will not expend any word about the Mana manipulating capabilities of the Prime arcana!<br /> And even if Sleepers are unable to store extra Mana in their unawakened souls, the Mana bounty received from a human soul sacrifice should be enough as a proof, don t you agree with me?<br /> Of course you do my dear.&quot;<br /> Lux, Obrimos and Mysterium member<br /> <br /> If you observe a God machine Angel with mage sight, what kind of information would you receive from each Arcana?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-14T20:15:16-07:00","id":1402903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1402704-as-a-mentor-a-question-get-a-watsonian-answer?p=1402861#post1402861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;<br /> If you observe a God machine Angel with mage sight, what kind of information would you receive from each Arcana?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think I can do fancy but, they are machine spirits rather merely spirits of machines, so maybe the Matter arcanum?<br /> <br /> Speaking of Matter, Promethean phenomena should fall under that purview. It's alchemy, it's transitional, it's thematic, it distinguishes prometheans while validating their woes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-14T21:16:12-07:00","id":1402911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1402704-as-a-mentor-a-question-get-a-watsonian-answer?p=1402861#post1402861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you observe a God machine Angel with mage sight, what kind of information would you receive from each Arcana?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;As my\u2026 <i>peculiar houseguest</i> has been quick to remind me, her erstwhile peers are as varied as anything one might draw out of the Inner Realms or the Shadow of the Earth; certain commonalities may be observed from their common origin, assuming their Fallen provenance and jealous creator do not prevent one from subjecting them to true scrutiny, but a skulking thing made to reconfigure the bodies interred in a particular cemetery will not yield the same information to the sight of Death as will a cat-shaped whisperer of carefully-selected lies to sleeping children, nor vice-versa with the eyes of the Mind.<br /> <br /> &quot;You may glean their missions and their maker, but the variety of tools at the Fallen Demiurge's belt and the complexity of its mechanisms are such that without a comprehensive look at the bigger picture, all you can know is that they are liars.&quot;<br /> <br /> Why do the Aeons pretend to be confined to the shores of Oroboros?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-15T00:18:52-07:00","id":1402918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1402704-as-a-mentor-a-question-get-a-watsonian-answer?p=1402911#post1402911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do the Aeons pretend to be confined to the shores of Oroboros?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Consider what they represent. They are the purest manifestations of the raw Arcana in the Fallen World. The highest conceptual space of the soul before the Abyss begins to dominate is really the <i>obvious </i>place for such understanding to reside. The distance from the rest of the world is representative of Quiessence, really, much as the Orobourus .represents the Abyss.&quot;<br /> -Nemo, Mastigos<br /> <br /> <br /> Why do deep cuts require a different practice than shallow cuts and bruising to repair?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-15T20:18:13-07:00","id":1403035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1402704-as-a-mentor-a-question-get-a-watsonian-answer?p=1402918#post1402918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do deep cuts require a different practice than shallow cuts and bruising to repair?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;They don't, both require the practice of Weaving to repair instantaneously. If by 'deep cuts' you mean the traumatic wounds caused by something like an arc welder or Mana infused Patterning spells, then that's because there is <i>no</i> natural pathway to healing those wounds.&quot;<br /> <br /> What is the most dangerous application of Knowing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-17T13:56:51-07:00","id":1403281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1402704-as-a-mentor-a-question-get-a-watsonian-answer?p=1403035#post1403035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the most dangerous application of Knowing?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;To find out secrets that someone will commit murder to protect.&quot; -Closed Lantern, Logophage","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-19T22:08:49-07:00","id":1403620,"title":"","content":"What are the pros and cons of getting a familiar? Jean-Babtiste Silver ladder acanthus and apprentice of spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7463-toine","name":"Toine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7463_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-20T14:21:17-07:00","id":1403714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1402704-as-a-mentor-a-question-get-a-watsonian-answer?p=1403620#post1403620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are the pros and cons of getting a familiar? Jean-Babtiste Silver ladder acanthus and apprentice of spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Its simple, you grow closer, that's it. Your pattern becomes their pattern, your mana their Essence, their senses are your senses. While physically you are divided, methaphysically you are the same.<br /> <br /> But this bond depends on mutual aid to exist, mutual understanding. Consider that for a moment, you must understand their single minded madness for Essence, cold rationality or closure, depending on the entity's nature. You must experience their obsessive drive to promote themselves across sympathetic space. <br /> <br /> What lies beyond your senses ? Will you be driven mad as you struggle to understand what is madness to us ? Will you find harmony with them by aligning enough of your mind with theirs to provide a clarity you never expected ? If you are too afraid to cross that line and confront whatever lies beyond, then you are not ready to have a familiar&quot; - Kubera, Mastigos archeomancer","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 07-20-2020, 07:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-20T15:20:00-07:00","id":1403720,"title":"","content":"The hypocrisy of the Free Council. It claims humanity is magical, that the Silver Ladder seeks to segregate the Awakened and the Sleeper, but does not attempt to Awaken individuals. Why do they do this? How do they not realize their own folly?- Hermes, new recruit of the Silver Ladder","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-20T22:41:58-07:00","id":1403765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1402704-as-a-mentor-a-question-get-a-watsonian-answer?p=1403720#post1403720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The hypocrisy of the Free Council. It claims humanity is magical, that the Silver Ladder seeks to segregate the Awakened and the Sleeper, but does not attempt to Awaken individuals. Why do they do this? How do they not realize their own folly?- Hermes, new recruit of the Silver Ladder</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;That's a bunch of fucking bullshit. Of course we attempt to Awaken Sleepers! But where you Diamond assholes look for individual humans you deem 'worthy' of the Truth, we Libertines know that the Truth needs maximum fucking dissemination on as many frequencies as possible: it's about Awakening <i>humanity</i> not some bullshit ass 'philosopher kings'.&quot; - Toymaker, Thaumatech Engineer and Libertine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-20T23:14:50-07:00","id":1403768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1402704-as-a-mentor-a-question-get-a-watsonian-answer?p=1403765#post1403765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &amp;quot;That's a bunch of fucking bullshit. Of course we attempt to Awaken Sleepers! But where you Diamond assholes look for individual humans you deem 'worthy' of the Truth, we Libertines know that the Truth needs maximum fucking dissemination on as many frequencies as possible: it's about Awakening <i>humanity</i> not some bullshit ass 'philosopher kings'.&amp;quot; - Toymaker, Thaumatech Engineer and Libertine.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was the exact kinda response I was hoping for lol. Love the Free Council.<br /> <br /> &quot;Why does the risk of Paradox increase on Inured spells? Is the mere act of Inuring a spell enough to make it susceptible to the Abyss?&quot;<br /> <br /> (Sorry I have not answered any question everyone. Being very new to the game, I really dont want to give a bad answer)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-21T07:12:47-07:00","id":1403804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1402704-as-a-mentor-a-question-get-a-watsonian-answer?p=1403768#post1403768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Why does the risk of Paradox increase on Inured spells? Is the mere act of Inuring a spell enough to make it susceptible to the Abyss?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;<i>All</i> spells are susceptible to the Abyss. As our insight grows, we see much more, so much more. Too much. Too much. Blind yourself with the burning torch and you may set fire to anything with its flame, but the fire spreads that much quicker. Close your heart to the hissing and popping and screaming \u2014 some noise is inevitable in our Fallen world. If staying in control of your magic is important to you, smother the stray sparks of its might in pure Truth, and cleave to the path of Sophia. The Abyss waits.&quot;<br /> - A recovering(?) Obrimos Nasnas.<br /> <br /> Why are Seers charged not to speak of the Gate?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-21T09:58:26-07:00","id":1403831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1402704-as-a-mentor-a-question-get-a-watsonian-answer?p=1403768#post1403768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Why does the risk of Paradox increase on Inured spells? Is the mere act of Inuring a spell enough to make it susceptible to the Abyss?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;I guess it's probably something to do with messing with your Sophia. Like, inuring causes a crack to form in it? I dunno.&quot;<br /> - Penny, Libertine Moros.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-21T12:48:16-07:00","id":1403867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1402704-as-a-mentor-a-question-get-a-watsonian-answer?p=1403804#post1403804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;<i>All</i> spells are susceptible to the Abyss. As our insight grows, we see much more, so much more. Too much. Too much. Blind yourself with the burning torch and you may set fire to anything with its flame, but the fire spreads that much quicker. Close your heart to the hissing and popping and screaming \u2014 some noise is inevitable in our Fallen world. If staying in control of your magic is important to you, smother the stray sparks of its might in pure Truth, and cleave to the path of Sophia. The Abyss waits.&quot;<br /> - A recovering(?) Obrimos Nasnas.<br /> <br /> Why are Seers charged not to speak of the Gate?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Hehehe...you are so green its almost hard to believe you made it this far. That is not a question you normally ask. Just because you are not a Seeer does not mean they couldn't call on secrets accords to have you vanished for even formulating that question. They are desperate to bury that name, they can and will sink to every depth imaginable to strike it from every tongue.<br /> <br /> But you did free me from the Conservatory in the Salt, so I owe you some measure of gratitude. Very well, I will indulge your curiosity.<br /> <br /> To speak of the Gate is to give it a meaning, an idea, to attribute it mandalas of significance and process it in the gears of reason. By introducing disorder into an already poorly calibrated and unhinged system, you are giving it a perch within your mind. From there it can exacerbate every error, multiply every bug and cause irreversible damage upon the already struggling clockwork of the universe. <br /> <br /> Even by the Tyrant's standards, her role encompasses a madness far more perverse than theirs. Until the day we have a better way to seal the Abyss, let her program run in the background, do not give it more priority or resources lest you unravel the entire computer.&quot; - Raktab\u012bja, Obrimos Timori","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}